// A bound C++ header that clang itself rejects must report the clang diagnostic and refuse the
// bind, not press on into the harvest and companion CodeGen. The fixture header declares a class
// with a field of an incomplete type and instantiates its own class template over it: the invalid
// record cascades into every instantiation that touches it, and walking that wreckage used to end
// in an access violation instead of an error message. The header includes no platform header, so
// it is equally broken under every standard library.
//
// Import-time diagnostic (raised during ProcessImports, before the listener walk), so the bare
// semicolon form at file scope arms the expectation before imports run.
expect_error("Nothing in it can be bound until that error is fixed");
import cpp "cpp_interop_broken.h";
